# Navigation Flow & Screen Architecture

## App Navigation Structure

```
SplashView (Entry Point)
├── WelcomeView (Unauthenticated)
│   ├── LoginView
│   │   └── TermsAndPrivacyView
│   └── SignupView
│       └── TermsAndPrivacyView
└── HomeView (Authenticated)
    ├── SettingView
    │   └── Various settings modals
    ├── EditSituationsView
    │   └── Add/Edit situation modals
    └── ItemListScreen
        └── Edit item functionality
```

## Screen Responsibilities

### Authentication Flow
- **[splash_view.dart](mdc:lib/splash_view.dart)**: Initial loading and auth state checking
- **[welcome_view.dart](mdc:lib/welcome_view.dart)**: Landing page for unauthenticated users
- **[login_veiw.dart](mdc:lib/screens/auth/login_veiw.dart)**: User login form
- **[signup_view.dart](mdc:lib/screens/auth/signup_view.dart)**: User registration form
- **[terms_and_privacy_view.dart](mdc:lib/screens/auth/terms_and_privacy_view.dart)**: Legal agreements

### Main Application Flow
- **[home_view.dart](mdc:lib/screens/home_view.dart)**: Main dashboard showing situations list
- **[item_list_screen.dart](mdc:lib/screens/item_list_screen.dart)**: Items within a specific situation
- **[edit_situations_view.dart](mdc:lib/screens/edit_situations_view.dart)**: Manage situations (add/edit/delete)
- **[setting_view.dart](mdc:lib/screens/setting_view.dart)**: App settings and user preferences

## Navigation Patterns

### Authentication Guards
Each protected screen checks authentication status:
```dart
final user = FirebaseAuth.instance.currentUser;
if (user == null) {
  Navigator.pushReplacement(
    context,
    MaterialPageRoute(builder: (context) => const WelcomeView()),
  );
}
```

### Navigation Methods
- **Standard Navigation**: `Navigator.push()` for normal screen transitions
- **Replacement Navigation**: `Navigator.pushReplacement()` for auth state changes
- **Modal Navigation**: Modal dialogs for forms and settings

### Data Passing
- **Route Parameters**: Pass objects like `Situation` between screens
- **User ID**: Extract from `FirebaseAuth.instance.currentUser?.uid`
- **Stream Data**: Real-time updates from Firestore

## State Persistence

### Authentication State
- Managed by [auth_provider.dart](mdc:lib/provider/auth_provider.dart)
- Listens to Firebase auth state changes
- Automatically updates UI when auth state changes

### Screen State
- Each screen has its own ViewModel for local state
- Shared state managed through Provider
- Data fetched from Firestore in real-time via streams

## Modal Workflows

### Add/Edit Operations
- Use modal dialogs from [add_modal.dart](mdc:lib/widgets/add_modal.dart)
- Helper functions in [item_modal_helper.dart](mdc:lib/screens/widget/item_modal_helper.dart)
- Notification settings modal in [show_notification_settings_modal.dart](mdc:lib/widgets/show_notification_settings_modal.dart)

### User Interactions
- Tap list items to navigate to detail screens
- Use floating action buttons for add operations
- Swipe gestures for item management
- Bottom sheet modals for quick actions

## Deep Linking & URL Handling

The app supports URL launching via [url_launcher](mdc:url_launcher) package for:
- External links from settings
- Terms and privacy policy links
- Help and support URLs

## Error Handling in Navigation

### Network Errors
- Show appropriate error messages
- Maintain navigation state during errors
- Retry mechanisms for failed operations

### Permission Errors
- Handle notification permission denials
- Guide users to system settings when needed
- Graceful degradation for missing permissions
